  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 115 PM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nMonday night through Saturday:\n\nThe extended models have good agreement with this period. A\nrobust upper trough will eject newd from the Pacific NW into the\nnrn high plains and Canadian Prairies early in the week. The\ndownstream upper ridge will begin to flatten and shift across \nthe Great Lakes on Tue in response to the low. The trailing cold\nfront to the occluded low over Canada will move across srn WI\nWed AM. Very warm and humid conditions will return ahead of the\nfront for Tue into Wed. PWATs will rise to nearly 2 inches once\nagain, while high temps well into the 80s will be possible.\nShowers and storm chances are at 50-80 percent for Tue nt. \n\nNwly flow aloft will briefly return afterward with a sfc ridge\nshifting across the wrn Great Lakes. Temps will return to near\nseasonal normals. Sly winds and warm, moist advection will\nreturn by the end of the week with an approaching sfc trough\nfrom the west. There are 20 percent chances for showers and\nstorms Fri nt-Sat at this time. \n\nGehring",
